# Trivy ignore list for the ai-workspace image scan job only (security.yml,
# matrix entry `image: ai-workspace`, wired via the trivy-action `trivyignores`
# input). Do not reuse this file for any other image's scan.
#
# Both entries below are reported by Trivy against files inside pip's own
# vendor tree (pip/_vendor/msgpack, pip/_vendor/pkg_resources) in the upstream
# `python:3.13-slim-bookworm` base image — NOT against anything installed from
# our requirements.lock (verified: `pip list` in the built image shows neither
# package). Trivy actually reads pip's bundled `bom.cdx.json`/`vendor.txt`
# SBOM metadata, which pins msgpack==1.1.2 and setuptools==70.3.0 as the
# versions pip vendors internally. `pip install msgpack>=1.2.1
# 'setuptools>=78.1.1'` was tried and confirmed NOT to clear these findings:
# it adds separate top-level packages alongside pip's vendored copies without
# touching the vendored code Trivy is actually scanning. The base image is
# already the newest available under this same digest (re-pulling the
# floating `python:3.13-slim-bookworm` tag on 2026-09-16 resolved to the same
# digest we pin), so there is no newer pip release to pick up here yet. This
# is upstream-controlled and gets revisited whenever the base image is bumped.
#
# msgpack: GHSA-6v7p-g79w-8964 (out-of-bounds read / crash on Unpacker reuse
# after certain errors) — fixed upstream in msgpack 1.2.1, vendored copy is
# 1.1.2.
GHSA-6v7p-g79w-8964

# setuptools: CVE-2025-47273 (path traversal in setuptools PackageIndex) —
# fixed upstream in setuptools 78.1.1, vendored copy (as pip/_vendor/pkg_resources)
# is 70.3.0. PackageIndex is a legacy easy_install code path we never invoke.
CVE-2025-47273

# urllib3: CVE-2026-97687 (HTTPS proxy TLS configuration may be ignored) and
# CVE-2026-97689 (unbounded chunk-size line buffering in read_chunked) —
# fixed upstream in urllib3 2.8.0, pip's vendored copy (pip/_vendor/urllib3)
# is 2.7.0. Same shape as the entries above: reported from pip's vendor SBOM,
# not from requirements.lock (urllib3 is not in it). Verified 2026-10-02: the
# newest pip on PyPI (26.2.1) and the newest `python:3.13-slim-bookworm`
# digest both still vendor urllib3 2.7.0, so there is nothing to bump to.
# pip only runs at image build time against hash-pinned wheels; analysis runs
# install nothing and the sandbox is created with `networkPolicy: 'deny-all'`,
# so neither the proxy path nor a hostile chunked response is reachable.
# Remove when a pip release vendors urllib3 >= 2.8.0 and the base is bumped.
CVE-2026-97687
CVE-2026-97689
